Yeah, they share the bad habit with Yahoo and other
big enterprises of sending back an auto-reply
_before_ reading your letter. It can be
disheartening to be sending them helpful comments,
and get back a big blast of spam as your first
reward.

On the good side, a human response is usually
forthcoming later, sometimes up to a week later.

Of course, the comments _I_ send them are only
helpful in a limited sense; the phrase "you are
still in need of adult supervision" is someplace
in probably each of my last twenty notes to them;
feel free to adopt it for your own use, maybe if
they see it more often they'll take the hint.

I took my own advice and sent them a comment on
their proportional type this evening, got the same
response you did.

The situation seems to have worstened, which I
hadn't realized before now since I only use Google
Groups when my preferred interface, the much easier
to read MailGate, is broken (don't bother, it's a
for-fee service now, I got my account there
grandfathered-in back when it was a free site
promising a lifetime free account to lure
participants who'd post articles with their little
ad at the bottom to attract more customers).

Now, any Google Groups search gets a groups-beta
reply, and I think any attempt to use Google Groups
at all became, within the past few hours, an instant
divert to the beta, but I'm not quite sure what I
saw meant that, since what you get is still clearly
labeled "beta".

The beta has lots more features, but I agree with
the comments here that the screen real-estate is
squandered, the left hand column stuff would be
better placed under the posting, like MailGate does
it, and also the shift to proportional type is a
show stopper for rgnr participants, since we do so
very much ASCII screenshot posting.

There may be a way to request "original format" and
get a view in fixed pitched type, but I haven't
found it yet, and that's a lot of trouble just to
see someone's ASCII art siggie unhashed, but would
be a way to see ascension maps if indeed the
"original format" feature exists somewhere in the
beta. I haven't tried the "options" button, it may
be in there.

